                <pb facs="0615" n="497" xml:id="pg497"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.512/750: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-01-21T11:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 21,
                                1928—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 2:45
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>45. My 32, January 16, 1 p.m. Following from consul general at Hankow: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“January 19, 4 p.m. My 5, January 14, 11 a.m. I have been informed
                            confidentially today that Bassett has been successful in his
                            negotiations and that contract calling for payment of 22½ percent on the
                            basis of customs valuations has been signed. Chinese authorities here
                            have agreed to postpone 50 percent tax until after China new year.
                            Probability is that companies concerned here will arrange compromise on
                            a basis of about 22½ percent.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
